26651-COMMENT ON TABLE public.premise_place_memberships IS
26652-    'v5.4.2-16 (places inventory P2-P7, P10, D1-D3). That a premise is within a place — or known to be outside it, with the distance where a law needs one (a positive finite number) — on an axis (regulatory: rate jurisdiction, franchise, customer law; tax: sales and local taxes), over a dated range, on dated evidence (an ordinance, the tax authority''s quarter, a commission order, an address lookup). No row means unknown, never outside. The axes are dated separately: one annexation is a regulatory membership from the ordinance date and a tax membership from the tax authority''s date (Texas Tax 321.102). place_kind and exclusivity_group are copied from the place''s kind at insert (not settable): within, at most one place per group per premise and axis at a time — one county; one of a city, its limited-purpose area or an extraterritorial area; districts stack. Written by the utility (RLS), under READ COMMITTED; never deleted; the only edits are a close (valid_to once, stamped) and a VOID for a row wrong from its first day (void_reason once, stamped) — a voided row is ignored by every exclusion, lookup, state guard and close floor, so the correct row can be recorded for the same days (review r2 S-b). The axes are independent: within a place on one axis and outside it on the other, over the same days, is accepted (D1). How the utility determined it (a boundary map, a geocoder) is outside the schema.';
26653-
26654--- The two edits a membership or profile takes (review r2 S-b): a close (its
26655--- end date, once) or a void (its reason, once — the row was wrong from its
26656--- first day); each stamped with when and who, nothing else changed. A voided
26657--- row takes no further edit.
26658:CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.place_citation_close_or_void(p_old anyelement, p_new anyelement, p_what text, p_end_col text)
26659-    RETURNS anyelement
26660-    LANGUAGE plpgsql
26661-    SET search_path = public, pg_temp
26662-    AS $$
26663-DECLARE
26664-    c_close_cols CONSTANT text[] := ARRAY[p_end_col, 'closed_at', 'closed_by'];
26665-    c_void_cols  CONSTANT text[] := ARRAY['void_reason', 'voided_at', 'voided_by'];
26666-    o jsonb := to_jsonb(p_old);
26667-    n jsonb := to_jsonb(p_new);
26668-    v_user jsonb;
26669-BEGIN
26670-    BEGIN
26671-        v_user := to_jsonb(NULLIF(current_setting('app.user_id', true), '')::uuid);
26672-    EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS THEN
26673-        v_user := 'null'::jsonb;
26674-    END;
26675-    IF o ->> 'voided_at' IS NOT NULL THEN
26676-        RAISE EXCEPTION USING
26677-            MESSAGE = format('%s %s: it was voided; a voided row takes no further edit (v5.4.2-16)', p_what, o ->> 'id'),
26678-            ERRCODE = 'restrict_violation';
26679-    END IF;
26680-    IF n ->> 'void_reason' IS NOT NULL THEN
26681-        IF (n - c_void_cols) <> (o - c_void_cols) OR (n ->> 'void_reason') !~ '[[:alnum:]]' THEN
26682-            RAISE EXCEPTION USING
26683-                MESSAGE = format('%s %s: a void states its reason and changes nothing else (v5.4.2-16)', p_what, o ->> 'id'),
26684-                ERRCODE = 'restrict_violation';
26685-        END IF;
26686-        RETURN jsonb_populate_record(p_new, jsonb_build_object('voided_at', now(), 'voided_by', v_user));
26687-    END IF;
26688-    IF o ->> p_end_col IS NOT NULL OR n ->> p_end_col IS NULL OR (n - c_close_cols) <> (o - c_close_cols) THEN
26689-        RAISE EXCEPTION USING
26690-            MESSAGE = format('%s %s: never edited — close it (%s, once, nothing else), void it with a reason if it was wrong from its first day, and record the correct row (v5.4.2-16)', p_what, o ->> 'id', p_end_col),
26691-            ERRCODE = 'restrict_violation';
26692-    END IF;
26693-    RETURN jsonb_populate_record(p_new, jsonb_build_object('closed_at', now(), 'closed_by', v_user));
26694-END;
26695-$$;
26696-COMMENT ON FUNCTION public.place_citation_close_or_void(anyelement, anyelement, text, text) IS
26697-    'v5.4.2-16 (review r2 S-b). The edit rule for a premise place membership or a utility service profile: a close (the end column set once, nothing else) or a void (void_reason set once, nothing else), each stamped with the time and the session''s user; a voided row takes no further edit. A closed row may still be voided (its close kept): a row wrong from its first day is wrong whether or not it has ended. The compared row is the whole row, so a client echoing every column must send the stored values.';
