32-- **-28 is mirrored now, ahead of -23, -25 and -26 in the board's queue (Ryan, 2026-11-04: "yes, mirror it now").** All three reviewers said ready on r2. The money patches were not ready to mirror: -23 is in round 9, and -25 and -26 are unreviewed. *Why:* none of the three redefines an object -28 changes (checked: the only shared mention is -23's list of rate-version triggers, which -28 does not touch), and CI had already passed the four together. Mirroring lets the four CIs be re-graded and lets -29 build on a settled base, instead of -28 waiting days or weeks behind patches still in review. *Why not keep the queue order:* the queue serialises mirrors that could conflict; these do not, and the board's rule already makes each later patch re-run its battery on the current `tally` before its own mirror. *Cost:* the money patches now apply over a `tu.sql` that carries -28 (they strict-apply cleanly on the new build). *Where it lives:* `sql/DEPLOY-VERIFICATION.md` (v5.4.2-28), the board's mirror queue note.
