42-## 2026-11-02 (-28 r1) — a consolidated bill is fixed once it goes out: every member bill final at issue, nothing attaches after (money stream's rule)
43-
44-- **A summary bill is issued only when every member bill is final, and no member bill attaches to it after it is issued (Ryan, 2026-11-02; option 1).** Round 1 of -28 (Codex B2, Opus N1, Fable N3) issued a consolidated parent while one child was still a draft, then moved that draft to an El Paso premise and attached a second child in another zone; both were accepted, and the parent's pipeline-safety fee, checked at issue, was afterwards refused on recheck. The schema already freezes an issued bill's own address and parent (`enforce_invoice_immutable`, CI-012), but per bill: nothing stops a summary going out over draft members, or a member joining a sent summary. *Why:* in practice a child's premise never moves (a service address is fixed) and a summary covers a known set of addresses; the reviewers' sequence is data entry no office does on purpose. Freezing the family at issue matches how a billing clerk already works, and it also keeps a sent summary's total equal to the bills it adds up, which matters more than the fee's day boundary. *Why not recheck the parent whenever a child changes (option 2):* a trigger on every invoice write to defend a state that should not exist, and it would refuse the child's write without saying why the family is closed. *Why not accept it (option 3):* the fee is small, but the same gap lets a summary's total drift from its members. *Where it lives:* invoices are the money stream's; sent as a board note (HANDOFF.md, rates → money, 2026-11-02). -28 states the gap as a known limit that the money stream's rule closes.
